# Per-customer manifests are produced by `assemble_scaffold.py --input ...` as
# `<customer>.manifest.jsonc`. They are NOT ignored: a real deploy package
# committed under customer/ must carry its exact manifest for provenance,
# alongside its input.json and rendered package/ (all three are committable —
# see ../NOTICE.md). Scratch `--check` experiments simply show as untracked in
# `git status`; don't `git add` the ones you don't mean to keep.
#
# (This dir previously ignored `*.manifest.jsonc` / `*.manifest.json`; that
# singled the manifest out from its already-committable siblings and is dropped.)
#
# SCOPE (#28, decided 2026-07-28): "committable" is about a PRIVATE deploy repo. A
# filled manifest carries tenantId, deploymentRootScope, logAnalyticsWorkspaceId and
# pacOwnerId. In THIS public repo the only tenant permitted is our own demo/lab tenant
# dlwaemsp.onmicrosoft.com (CSP-covered); a client's manifest goes in the client's own
# private repo. Not enforced by this file on purpose -- an ignore rule cannot tell one
# tenant's GUID from another's, and a rule that silently drops files people were told
# to commit is worse than a rule they can read. See ../NOTICE.md.
